                "text": "To solve  \n\\[\n\\sin(x)+x^2=42 \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad f(x)=\\sin(x)+x^2-42=0,\n\\]\nwe find the real roots numerically.\n\nUsing a root-finder on \\(f(x)\\), there are **two** real solutions:\n\\[\nx \\approx -6.49709821697\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\approx \\phantom{-}6.46665004091\n\\]\n\n(These work because \\(x^2\\) must be close to \\(42\\), so \\(x\\) is near \\(\\pm\\sqrt{42}\\approx \\pm 6.4807\\), with a small adjustment from \\(\\sin(x)\\).)",
